/// Activation height for the station **ownership-binding** rules (#2742 +
/// #2743) — one constant on purpose, because the two rules are one semantic:
/// `owner_address` becomes cryptographically verified (#2742) at the same
/// height it becomes load-bearing for payment (#2743). Routing money by the
/// field without verifying it, or verifying it without using it, are each
/// worse than either alone.
///
/// From this height:
/// - a `StationRegistration` only authorizes if `owner_pubkey` derives to
///   `owner_address` under the canonical `PublicKey::to_address` derivation
///   (SHA3-256 over the raw ed25519 public key, first 20 bytes);
/// - contribution/forecast rewards pay the **registered station owner**, not
///   whatever address the reveal transaction's first output names.
///
/// NOT zero, unlike the constants above: those activated at a fresh genesis
/// cut, while this rule strengthens a chain that already carries
/// registrations (block 674) and paid reward records (blocks 716, 851) whose
/// replay must stay byte-identical under the pre-activation branch. **The
/// value must exceed the live chain tip at the moment upgraded binaries are
/// running on every node.**
///
/// History: owner set 11_000 on 2026-08-06 for the original testnet (chain 777),
/// when its measured tip was **1582**.
///
/// **Owner ruling 2026-10-23: 3_000 for chain 888** (the public testnet, new genesis
/// 2026-10-22), measured at about h1076 with about 77 s per block. Every 888 node must
/// run a binary carrying this value before 888 reaches 3_000; a node still running an
/// older binary (11_000) at that height computes different rewards and forks.
///
/// This constant is chain-agnostic: on a chain that already passed h3_000 under the
/// 11_000 rule (chain 777), blocks 3_000..11_000 no longer replay byte-identically
/// with this binary.
///
/// **Do not derive that window from `BLOCK_TIME_PROGRESSION`.** The table's
/// `(1_000, 7_200)` band is the consensus *target* for this height range, and on
/// the live testnet it is inert: blocks are driven by the collector polling
/// `launch_api::routes::mining` on a ~60 s loop, which outruns the target. Two
/// independent reviewers computed this window wrong from constants alone — 300 s
/// gave "57 hours", 7_200 s gave "57 days", and the measured cadence is 60 s.
/// Measure the live chain instead:
///
/// ```text
/// ssh <operator>@<node-host> 'docker logs --since 12m wrfcoin-testnet-node' | grep "Mined block"
/// ```
///
/// (Use your authorized operator access path; reachability is installation-specific.)
pub const STATION_OWNERSHIP_BINDING_ACTIVATION_HEIGHT: u64 = 3_000;

/// Height at which contribution scoring accepts the rich, mixed-type Ambient
/// weather payload used by the production collectors (#2768).
///
/// This deliberately co-activates with station ownership binding. A positive
/// reward must never become possible before the registered station owner is
/// the consensus-selected payee. Below this height the strict legacy
/// `FxHashMap<String, f64>` parser remains byte-for-byte authoritative for
/// replay of the existing testnet history.
pub const RICH_AMBIENT_REWARD_ACTIVATION_HEIGHT: u64 = STATION_OWNERSHIP_BINDING_ACTIVATION_HEIGHT;

